Fix real upstream gaps (not AXOS features): eight functions are called from
rc/rc.c, rc/init.c, rc/wan.c, and rc/sysdeps/init-broadcom.c with no
implementation anywhere in this Merlin release's source tree, and no
GT-AX6000 prebuilt object provides them either (checked every
rc/prebuild/GT-AX6000/*.o with `nm`). Each was confirmed via a real build
attempt: `make gt-ax6000` fails linking `rc` with "undefined reference to"
each of these symbols.

- chk_acscli2_cmds(), avbl_reset_exclvalid() (rc.c, rctest_main): debug-only
  handlers for the manual "rc chk_acsc"/"rc acsc" CLI test commands, not
  called from any boot/runtime path. Guarded out (the debug commands become
  no-ops); nothing else depends on them.

- chk_acscli2_cmds() (sysdeps/init-broadcom.c, init_syspara): a second,
  separate call site for the same missing function, under a different guard
  (RTCONFIG_AMAS alone, no BCMWL6 check) — easy to miss since it's a
  different file. Guarded out the same way.

- nordvpn_main() (rc.c, applets[] table): only wires up the "/sbin/nordvpn"
  CLI convenience symlink to `rc`. Actual NordVPN client configuration goes
  through shared/vpn_utils.c and rc/vpnc_fusion.c's VPNC_PROTO_NORDVPN
  dispatch, neither of which needs this applet entry. Guarded out.

- noasusddns() (init.c, init_nvram2): declared `extern` only under
  RTCONFIG_TCODE but called completely unconditionally. RTCONFIG_TCODE is
  genuinely on for this router, so this is not merely a guard mismatch — no
  implementation exists at all, TCODE on or off. Always take the
  WWW.ASUS.COM.CN-only branch of the original OR condition.

- check_wlx_nband_type() (init.c, WLAN startup path): no declaration at all
  anywhere, called completely unguarded. Guarded out with `#if 0` — no
  existing flag in this codebase corresponds to whatever this was meant to
  gate.

- get_jpix_map(), get_ocn_map() (wan.c, wan6_up, RTCONFIG_SOFTWIRE46's
  WAN_V6PLUS/WAN_V6OPTION/WAN_OCNVC MAP-E cases): only reachable when the
  ISP's "dhcpenble_x" NVRAM flag requests DHCP-auto-fetched Japan-ISP
  (JPIX/OCN) map rules. Guarded out; falls through to the static map-e path
  below (the same path taken when dhcpenble_x is unset), rather than the
  auto-fetch this router cannot actually provide.

`git apply --check`-verified against the pinned tag (3004.388.9), applied on
top of 0001-0004. Not yet verified past that point in a completed build —
see docs/build-environment.md and docs/ROADMAP.md.

